#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD2246 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "The NARMS record carries the whole number '2' in TSVAL, so the numeric requirement holds. Row 2 carries a non-numeric TSVAL but under a different TSPARMCD, which is outside this rule's condition. (Positive control added by PLAN-absent-guard-test-hardening P3: PMDA-SD2246 previously had ONLY an expect=skipped fixture, which asserts non-execution and so proved nothing about the rule ever running. Modelled on its twin FDA-SD2246.)"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | NARMS | Planned Number of Arms | 2
S1 | TS | 2 | ACTSUB | Actual Number of Subjects | TWO
